WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.341
Slice one point two gives Christian Fitness its backend, closed until you sign in.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.389
Five projects, one direction. Domain holds the entities, Application the rules and

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:18.778
the seeds, Infrastructure speaks to Postgres, and the API and the command line sit

00:00:18.778 --> 00:00:19.538
on top.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.376
Health answers anyone, in one word. Live means the process runs; ready means the

00:00:25.376 --> 00:00:26.819
database answers.

00:00:27.019 --> 00:00:30.292
Here there is none, so it says unhealthy, and nothing more.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.470
Everything else needs a session. Without one, the answer is a 401, as ProblemDetails

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:42.589
with a code the screens can branch on, even for a path that doesn't exist.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.737
An unexpected error becomes a plain 500, code server_error: no message, no stack

00:00:49.737 --> 00:00:50.467
trace.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.176
Open Telemetry records each request by its route template, method and status.

00:00:57.376 --> 00:01:01.752
The path, the query string and anything personal are dropped before export.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.982
The API never migrates. cf migrate applies the schema, and cf seed adds the first

00:01:09.982 --> 00:01:14.344
admin from settings. Run it twice, and nothing changes.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.031
Every rule failed first, then passed: twenty-one tests, and no real database.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.003
That's slice one point two. Christian Fitness: a Christian community for health in

00:01:29.003 --> 00:01:30.279
body and spirit.
